{"symbol":"GVS.MI","area":"europe","updated":"2026-11-16T19:18:56Z","info":{"address1":"Via Roma 50","address2":"Zona Industriale","city":"Zola Predosa","state":"BO","zip":"40069","country":"Italy","phone":"39 0516 17 63 11","fax":"39 0516 17 62 00","website":"https://www.gvs.com","industry":"Pollution & Treatment Controls","industryKey":"pollution-treatment-controls","industryDisp":"Pollution & Treatment Controls","sector":"Industrials","sectorKey":"industrials","sectorDisp":"Industrials","longBusinessSummary":"GVS S.p.A., together with its subsidiaries, produces and sells filter solutions for applications in the healthcare and life sciences, energy and mobility, and health and safety sectors in Italy and internationally. The company offers health and safety products, such as hand dryer and vacuum cleaner filters; nailstation COSMO products; fume extraction and HVAC building products; and disposable masks, half masks, integra masks, powered air purifying respirators, face fit testing, replacement filters, supplied air respirators, spare parts, and accessories. It also provides autoclave filters, insufflation and ventilation filters and kits, machine filters, respiratory and anesthesia filters, smoke evacuation filters and kits, spirometry filters and accessories, suction filters, and tracheal humidifier filters; healthcare liquid products, such as bacterial air vents, blood tubular filters, infusion disc filters, IV and liquid filters, IV flow regulators, medical bags and components, sterile infusion sets and accessories, stopcock and manifold products, and transducer protectors; and capsule and cartridge filters, disc and sheet membranes, mini roll membranes, DNA/RNA test kits, filter papers, microbiology products, microfiltration devices, microporous and track etched roll membranes, protein microarrays, and environmental monitoring products, as well as western blotting membranes and reagents. In addition, the company offers energy and mobility products, such as fuel tanks and pumps, metal components, reservoirs, and SCR urea systems; ABS, ESP, and brake systems; EV applications and batteries; injection, tank vapour ventilation, and transmission products; ventilation systems; and cabin air and HVAC systems, and engine air intake ventilation filters. The company was formerly known as GVS S.r.l. and changed its name to GVS S.p.A. in 2001. GVS S.p.A. was founded in 1979 and is headquartered in Zola Predosa, Italy. GVS S.p.A. operates as a subsidiary of GVS Group S.r.l.","fullTimeEmployees":3930,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Massimo  Scagliarini","age":60,"title":"CEO & Director","yearBorn":1965,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Marco  Pacini","age":54,"title":"CFO & Non Executive Director","yearBorn":1971,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Matteo  Viola","age":51,"title":"Chief Operating Officer","yearBorn":1974,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Guido  Bacchelli","title":"Head of Strategy, Corporate Development & IR","exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Rozemaria  Bala","age":44,"title":"General Counsel","yearBorn":1981,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Andrea  Zanaboni","age":51,"title":"Chief Marketing Officer","yearBorn":1974,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Paola  Musuraca","age":38,"title":"Corporate HR Director","yearBorn":1987,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0}],"executiveTeam":[],"maxAge":86400,"priceHint":2,"previousClose":6.23,"open":6.22,"dayLow":6.08,"dayHigh":6.31,"regularMarketPreviousClose":6.23,"regularMarketOpen":6.22,"regularMarketDayLow":6.08,"regularMarketDayHigh":6.31,"dividendYield":0,"exDividendDate":1624233600,"payoutRatio":0,"beta":1.006,"trailingPE":26.1304,"forwardPE":19.4687,"volume":81164,"regularMarketVolume":81164,"averageVolume":105511,"averageVolume10days":178500,"averageDailyVolume10Day":178500,"bid"